<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#fur-trade">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fur trade</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as furs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fur trade was the commerce in animal pelts, highly valued for clothing and as luxury goods. Furs from the northern forests passed through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, financed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> expansion across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a>, and were central to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-france">New France</a>, the core of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fur-trade.jpg" alt="Fur trade" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown / --Kuerschner 16:04, 24 March 2008 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Irbit_-_Fur_market.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
